WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome back, everybody. We are
hanging out with Michelle Obama.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:05.234
Now, Michelle, since
so many people look up to you,

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.667
I thought
that you could help settle

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:09.868
some of the biggest and most
important debates of all time.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:12.367
We did this with President
Obama, and it was a lot of fun.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.000
Are you ready for this?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.367
-I will do my best.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:18.901
-Let's do it. It is time
for "Michelle Obama Settles It."

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.300
-♪ Michelle Obama
settles it ♪

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.934
♪ Michelle Obama settles it ♪

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:29.167
-Alright. Here we go. Ready?

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:33.033
Is iced coffee
only for the summer?

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.868
-Yes. Absolutely.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.033
-Yeah, I kind of -- Yeah.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.300
Yeah. I agree.
-I mean --

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.701
-There you go. Next.

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:43.133
Is it wrong to re-gift?

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.901
-It is.
-Yeah, I agree.

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:47.934
-You know, it's kind of lazy.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:50.067
-It is, right? Yeah.
Yeah. I agree.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.000
And if you don't want it,
you can donate it or something,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.934
but don't re-gift it.
-Yeah, yeah, give it away,

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:56.200
but don't -- you know,
literally give it away.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.501
Don't gift it away.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:58.934
-I totally agree with you.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:02.734
Is it rude to respond
to a text with "K"?

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:05.033
-It depends on the age. Right?

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:08.734
If you respond to young people
with more than "K,"

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:11.601
then they think
you're mad at them. You know?

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.601
If you use words
and punctuations,

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.901
I was told, "Mom,
why are you mad at me?

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.734
You used a period."

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.167
And it's like, "Well,
that's called grammar."

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.701
-Alright, a lot of people are
talking about this next one.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:26.000
Middle part or side part?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.033
-Uh, duh!

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.501
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:29.968
Side part, yeah. I agree.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.968
This one may be controversial.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.000
Best meal --
Breakfast, lunch or dinner?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.000
I think I know your answer.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.067
-Dinner.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.300
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.634
It's dinner. Yeah.
-You think that? Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.067
Breakfast and lunch
are throwaways.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.267
-Right? They're fine.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.701
Lunch is definitely
just all business for me.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:48.767
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:49.868
-Breakfast now and then.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:52.167
But dinner, you have memories.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.033
You have conversations.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.734
-It's bigger.
-You can have wine.

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:57.267
-You can have wine.
You can have a cocktail.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:58.567
It's unbelievable.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:00.467
Oh, yeah, dinner all the way.
I knew it.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.501
Next up, I know
the answer to this.

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:04.701
Pancakes or waffles?

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.133
-Waffles!

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.734
-You have to, yeah.
You have to, yeah.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.334
-Yeah.
-Yeah, you're right.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:12.400
Should you wet your toothbrush
before putting toothpaste on it?

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.601
-Absolutely.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.467
-Yeah. Yes! You --

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.701
You're going to go dry in there?

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:20.367
-Yeah. You know,
you can cut up your gums and --

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.501
-It's disrespectful
to your teeth.

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:23.934
-Too harsh. It's too harsh.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.968
-It's too much.
Too much -- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:28.400
Should you floss
before or after brushing?

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.200
-I floss after, because
that's what the dentist does

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.767
when you go in for a cleaning.
They always floss last.

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:38.634
So I figure they know something,
so I'm going to do what they do.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.234
-Yeah. I'm trying to think
of what I do.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:41.367
Yeah, I guess so.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:42.567
-But have you
been to the dentist?

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:43.968
You been to the dentist lately?

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:46.367
-I love going to the dentist.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.267
-What's wrong with you?

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:51.334
-I love it. I think it's --
I feel great when I leave.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.067
I feel -- Clean teeth.

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:55.801
I love it. I don't need gas --
I'm so good.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.000
I love it.
-Really? That's so cute.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.334
-I love it.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:00.901
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:03.968
Next up, oh, next one
is about "The Crown."

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:06.634
Season 1 or Season 3?

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:09.367
-Season 1. Season 1.
That was where it all began.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:12.701
That's where "The Crown" became
"The Crown," after that season.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:16.467
-Alright, who gets to pick
the music, driver or passenger?

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.167
-Driver, all the way.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.000
You're doing the work.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.534
You get to control
the sound system.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.567
-No.

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.000
-You -- No?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.501
-I think passenger, 'cause then
you can get in there there

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:28.701
and you start
looking through things

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.834
and you start making
a good deejay set list.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.767
-No, but I want
the driver happy and awake.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.467
-Yeah, I totally --
I take it back, yes.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.667
Alright. Next, corn.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.734
On the cob or off the cob?

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:40.767
-On the cob!

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.567
-On the cob -- This is insane.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.234
I'm sorry to even
ask that question.

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:46.601
Of course. No question.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:50.801
Next, we have,
"Is a wok a pot or a pan?"

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.467
-Pan.
-Pan. Yeah.

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.133
This is the best question
coming up.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.534
Ready for this? This is
the best question coming up.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:01.167
Better movie,
"Taxi" or "Fever Pitch"?

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:02.868
-"Taxi."

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.634
But I've seen neither.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:07.167
-What are you talking about?

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.934
You -- No, don't you even dare.

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.467
What are you -- I was --

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:15.200
-I've been busy! I've been busy!

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.501
-It's me and Queen Latifah!

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.567
You had to --

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:21.801
-That's why I picked it, "Taxi."

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.367
I'm sure I would like that one.

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:25.000
-Oh, my goodness.
You haven't seen either.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.667
Can I tell you a quick story?

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:31.601
-Please.
-I got a --

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:34.601
Ann Curry brought me --
was on Air Force One,

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:36.067
and she brought back

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:39.534
the movie selection card
from Air Force One,

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:42.200
because "Taxi" was on there.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.767
And so I was very excited.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:48.467
-So you just assume because Ann
Curry had it on Air Force One

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.200
that everybody saw it?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.467
-Well, I'm assuming
you were probably there,

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:53.901
and that was
one of your options.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:55.667
The whole family loves "Taxi."

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.968
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.901
I got to get you a DVD.
-That's why it was in the back

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.467
where you all would sit.
It wasn't up in our cabin.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:03.734
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:06.133
Okay. Here's a good one here.

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:10.501
How do you pronounce the word
at the bottom of my screen?

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:11.634
-"Geero."

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:13.601
-Yes! That is correct!

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.434
That -- I just learned that.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.334
I would say "jairo."
-As opposed to "jairo"?

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:18.634
-"Jairo."
-A "jeero"?

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:19.968
That's how my dad said it.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:21.734
-It's "geero," is right.
-We're gonna get some "jairos."

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:23.567
-It's "geero" --
Yep, I used to say "jairo."

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:24.767
And it -- You're right.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:27.367
And finally, better way
to end an e-mail,

00:05:27.367 --> 00:05:29.567
sincerely or yours truly?

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.667
-Ooh.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:35.067
I usually say "all the best."

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:38.400
But I'd say maybe sincerely
to keep it short.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.033
-You guys heard it here first.

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:42.567
All the best to you.

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:44.467
My thanks to Michelle Obama

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:46.701
for settling
these important debates.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:49.467
Her show, "Waffles + Mochi,"
streaming now on Netflix.

